PARITY SUMMARY
  The web XRayHeader is a three-StatCard header strip inside a Grid cols={{ default: 1, sm: 3 }}:
    1. Total samples   = loading ? '—' : fmtInt(data?.total_samples ?? 0)   (Activity icon, "within selected window")
    2. Distinct fields = loading ? '—' : fmtInt(data?.unique_fields ?? 0)   (Layers icon,   "unique signal names")
    3. Window          = WINDOW_LABEL[windowSel]                            (Clock icon,    "observation horizon")
  Native port reproduces all three tiles, the fmtInt locale-grouped integer, the WINDOW_LABEL echo for every
  window (5m/15m/1h/6h/24h), and every t() key verbatim (admin.xray.stats.* + admin.xray.windowLabel.*).
  The responsive Grid (default:1 / sm:3) maps to ViewThatFits(.horizontal): 3-up when wide, 1-up stacked
  when compact. Data is bound through XRayHeaderModel (P1/S8 seam mirroring LoadableState / LiveConnectionState);
  no HTTP in the view. P1/S11 view.opened telemetry fires once on appear with slug "XRayHeader".

STATES (every state renders — none hidden behind a null guard)
  loading  → numeric tiles skeleton, window tile shows its label (operator selection is known pre-fetch)
  content  → three tiles with values
  empty    → friendly empty note + the three tiles (zeros), never a blank box (web zeros = empty)
  error    → QueryError-equivalent panel + Retry affordance (model.refresh)
  stale    → freshness banner ("counts may be stale") + cached tiles + one auto-refresh on entering stale
  offline  → freshness banner ("showing the last loaded counts") + cached tiles

